        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm/dist/cli.js",
        "Link reference definitions such as '[link]: https://example.com \"title\"' are consumed by the lexer and recorded in lexer.links, but they do not appear in the token array returned by marked.lexer(), so walkTokens and token-based extensions cannot see them. Expose each definition as a block token of type \"def\" with fields raw, tag (the normalized label), href and title (undefined when absent), placed at its position in the token stream. Rendered output must not change: the parser must render nothing for the new token by default, through a new overridable renderer method def(token) so custom renderers can emit something for definitions. Every existing spec example must still pass. Source lives under src/ (TypeScript); the library is built with npm run build:esbuild before tests run.\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npm run build:esbuild && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
